# Release hygiene — `git archive HEAD` builds the install zip, so every tracked
# path lands in the package unless it is export-ignore'd here. These paths are
# versioned for development/CI/collaboration but are NOT needed to run the
# plugin on a Moodle site.
#
# The Svelte case is the one to get right: svelte/build/ SHIPS (it is the
# compiled mailbox the browser loads, and view.php resolves it through
# svelte/build/manifest.json), while svelte/src/ and the whole toolchain do not.
# Nothing in CI rebuilds that bundle, so it is a committed artefact like
# amd/build/ and must never be export-ignore'd.
#
# Two deliberate exceptions to the fleet baseline, both upstream artefacts that
# README.md links to and which would leave dangling references if stripped:
#   - LICENSES/ SHIPS: upstream's REUSE-style licence texts.
#   - CONTRIBUTING.md SHIPS.
# tests/ also SHIPS, per Moodle convention.
#
# Verify with:  git check-attr export-ignore -- <path>
# (a path marked "set" is excluded from the archive; "unspecified" ships).

/.claude               export-ignore
/.DS_Store             export-ignore
/.gitattributes        export-ignore
/.github               export-ignore
/.gitignore            export-ignore
/.phpcs.xml            export-ignore
/.prettierrc           export-ignore
/.vscode               export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md             export-ignore

svelte/.gitignore      export-ignore
svelte/.prettierignore export-ignore
svelte/.prettierrc     export-ignore
svelte/eslint.config.js export-ignore
svelte/package-lock.json export-ignore
svelte/package.json    export-ignore
svelte/src             export-ignore
svelte/svelte.config.js export-ignore
svelte/tsconfig.json   export-ignore
svelte/vite.config.js  export-ignore
